{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "We have only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), giving us essentially no information about whether the image modality contributes useful signal. The most critical uncertainty to resolve before committing budget to multimodal or encoder variations is whether image features alone are informative for this task. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is a clean, single-variable comparison against our existing RNA-only baseline: it isolates the image modality's contribution using a standard, well-understood encoder. If image-only accuracy is comparable to RNA-only (~48%), it suggests neither modality is sufficient alone and multimodal fusion is essential. If image-only is substantially higher, it redirects our search toward image encoders and multimodal fusion strategies. If substantially lower, it confirms RNA as the primary signal and justifies focusing on RNA encoder upgrades (scvi, scgpt) and multiprofile aggregation. This experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most fundamental design axis (modality) before we spend budget on more complex multimodal or encoder configurations."
}

